            <div xml:id="d688-a1">

                <pb facs="1254" n="1130" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg1130"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 383.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr.
                            Droz.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 29,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, chargé d’affaires of the United States of America, has the
                    honor, referring to his note of March 23, 1881, respecting the shipment of
                    Fridolina Vögelin and Theresa Hauser, notorious and depraved prostitutes, whose
                    journey was paid to New York by their native commune of Böttstein, canton
                    Argovie, to inform his excellency Mr. Droz, President of the Swiss Confederation
                    and the High Federal Council, that the steamship Suevia arrived yesterday at New
                    York.</p>
                <p>The undersigned renews the expression of the hope that the High Federal Council
                    will cause these women to be returned to Switzerland as promptly as possible,
                    and that in future similar action on the part of the local authorities in this
                    country may be prevented.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails himself of this occasion to renew to his excellency Mr.
                    Droz, President of the Swiss Confederation, and to the High Federal Council, the
                    assurances of his most distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>NICHOLAS FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
